Key findings vs spec.md §4.2/§8/§9.1 predictions:
- sssd.conf ipa_server line matches predicted shape exactly:
    ipa_server = _srv_, ipa1.ipa.pilot.internal, ipa2.ipa.pilot.internal
- krb5.conf duplicates all four of kdc/master_kdc/admin_server/kpasswd_server (spec only
  anticipated kdc/admin_server/kpasswd_server; installer also emits a second master_kdc line).
  No --fixed-primary was passed; installer never adds it on its own.
- default.conf's `server`/`xmlrpc_uri` fields remain PINNED TO ipa1 ONLY, even in 2-server
  enrollment (`server = ipa1.ipa.pilot.internal`, `xmlrpc_uri = https://ipa1.ipa.pilot.internal/ipa/xml`).
  This confirms spec.md §13's concern: any Pilot `ipa` CLI invocation that relies on
  /etc/ipa/default.conf's default reader (no override) stays pinned to ipa1 regardless of
  client HA state — Phase 5 admin-endpoint selection is a real, not theoretical, gap.
